    "The organization of public space, including street furniture, lighting, shading, and movement, has an important role in reducing stress.",
    "Green areas and water features are vital components to decrease stress due to their calm psychological effect and role in reducing noise.",
    "Separation of traffic between vehicles and pedestrians can create safe and smooth movement spaces.",
    "The social dimension of public space, supporting activities like talking, walking, playing, eating, drinking, and watching, enhances public space and promotes enjoyment and happiness.",
    "Architects, urban space designers, and planners should create urban life for people as non-stressed psychological public spaces."
